# AnonOS MVP - Time Synchronization Strategy
#
# Current approach:
# - Firewall blocks outbound UDP port 123 (NTP) to prevent cleartext time leaks.
# - systemd-timesyncd is present but may fail to sync until Tor is established.
# - Tor can bootstrap without perfect time in most cases.
#
# Future hardening:
# - Replace NTP with sdwdate fetching time over Tor from multiple sources.
#
# For this MVP, time leaks are mitigated by:
# 1. UTC timezone (no local timezone leak).
# 2. No persistent RTC storage on live media (reboot resets clock).
# 3. nftables blocks NTP egress, preventing direct time queries.
